            "Must obtain the master's degree within the award period, or 54 ECTS in year one for a two-year programme, to receive the final EUR 1,525 instalment",
            "Must not combine the Master Mind scholarship with another Flemish Government scholarship, an Erasmus+ or Erasmus Mundus scholarship, a BAEF scholarship or a Fullbright scholarship",
            "At least half of the master's programme credits must be obtained at the Flemish host institution",
            "On completion of the mobility, must submit an essay in the provided format and complete a short questionnaire about the mobility",
            "If the scholarship is lost, must pay the full tuition fee to continue the programme"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "Priority-country reserved scholarships: Japan (3), Mexico (3), Palestine (2) and USA (5)",
            "Borse Ateneo equivalent funding is not mentioned; this is the Flemish government Master Mind programme administered through host institutions",
            "Annex 2 of the call contains further detail on credit requirements, and Annex 1 explains how to calculate the American GPA",
            "The scholarship is currently under review by the Flemish Ministry of Education for academic year 2027-2028"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "VLUHR International - Master Mind Scholarships: mastermind@vluhr.be; Huis Hoger Onderwijs - Sinter-Goedeleplein 14, 1000 Brussels, Belgium; international@vluhr.be"
          },
          "description": "Master Mind Scholarships are granted by the Flemish government to excellent students who want to follow a master's programme at a Flemish higher education institution, to promote Flemish higher education as a top study destination for international talent. The total budget for 2026-2027 is EUR 480,000 and an estimated 30 international students can benefit, with a maximum award of EUR 10,225 per academic year for one year (60 ECTS) or two years (120 ECTS). Applicants must have a GPA of 3.5 out of 4.0 and the stated English proficiency, be nominated by a single host institution, and have their file submitted through Mobility-Online by 27 April 2026 at 23h59 GMT+1.",
          "program_type": "Regional government master's scholarship (Flanders, Belgium)",
          "region": "Belgium (Flanders and Brussels)",
          "coverage": "Provides a maximum of EUR 10,225 per academic year as a cash award, with the host institution permitted to charge a tuition fee of EUR 136.50 for 2026-2027, but does not cover tuition fees, accommodation, living costs beyond the award, or travel.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Convert your GPA to a 3.5 out of 4.0 scale using the published method on the last obtained bachelor's or master's degree",
            "Take IELTS or TOEFL no more than 3 years before the April application processing date, at 7.0/94/C1 for a standard programme or 6.5/90/B2 for a School of Arts programme",
            "Apply to the chosen Flemish host institution by its own deadline, which precedes the central 27 April date",
            "Ensure only one Flemish institution nominates you",
            "Get certified translations of any transcript or diploma not in Dutch, French, German or English",
            "Ask your referees for two signed English recommendation letters",
            "Plan the credit split so at least half the master's credits are earned at the Flemish host institution",
            "Do not hold an Erasmus+, Erasmus Mundus, BAEF, Fullbright or other Flemish Government scholarship"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Missing the host institution's internal deadline, which is earlier than 27 April",
            "Not being nominated, or being nominated by more than one institution",
            "GPA below 3.5 out of 4.0",
            "English test older than 3 years at the April processing date, or below the required band",
            "Failing the host institution's academic check or not being accepted",
            "Enrolling in a preparatory, bridging or distance learning programme",
            "Not being accepted by the host institution even if selected, since acceptance is a condition",
            "Failing to obtain the degree or 54 ECTS and thereby losing the final EUR 1,525"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Tuition fees beyond the EUR 136.50 the host institution may charge",
            "Accommodation",
            "Living costs beyond EUR 10,225 per academic year",
            "Travel to and from Belgium",
            "Visa and immigration costs"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Verify your GPA conversion follows the published American GPA calculation annex",
            "Check every document is in Dutch, French, German or English or has a certified translation attached",
            "Confirm both recommendation letters are signed and written in English",
            "Ensure the CV includes your GPA out of 4.0 and any publications, awards or previous scholarships",
            "Check the English test date is within 3 years of the April processing date",
            "Confirm your passport or national ID copy is legible"
          ],
