          },
          "description": "The Willem F. Duisenberg Fellowship at NIAS lets researchers and policymakers work on applied monetary economics, macroeconomics and public finance for five to ten months. It is open to prominent mid- to late-career researchers and to promising early-career talents from the Netherlands or abroad, with a minimum of three years of post-PhD experience required, and the Foundation gives particular priority to researchers with an outstanding record in those fields. Fellows receive a personal stipend, or a Dutch University Grant if affiliated with a Dutch university or research institute, plus subsidised housing where eligible or reimbursement of local public transport. The 2027-2028 call ran from 15 January to 13 April 2026 and has closed.",
