          "description": "The SNSF Starting Grants are the SNSF's highest level of career funding, enabling researchers to carry out their own independent project and lead a research team in Switzerland. Applicants can request a budget of up to 1 million francs for project funding over five years and can additionally apply for funds to cover their own salary. Eligibility requires a doctorate (or equivalent or medical degree), falling within the eligibility window, not yet having achieved the objective of the call, and a Swiss link of at least two years of research at an average of at least 80% worktime. Evaluation is a two-phase, competition-based procedure with external peer review and interviews.",
