          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm your doctorate defence date puts you inside the eligibility window (for StG2026 calculated until 1 February 2026)",
            "Confirm you do not already lead a research group of 2-3 people or hold a position with significant third-party funding",
            "Confirm you have no approved or ongoing PRIMA, Eccellenza, SNSF Starting Grant, ERC Starting Grant or Practice-to Science",
            "Document your Swiss link: at least two years of research at an average of at least 80% FTE, or at least 19.2 months total",
            "Check whether an individual SNSF Project Funding grant would disqualify you (it would; a collaborative one approved before 1 April 2026 would not)",
            "Confirm your host institution will sign the 2026 confirmation letter template",
            "Decide whether to request your own salary and at what level (assistant professor, or group leader at institutions without assistant professorship posts)",
            "Check your employment and work-time percentages against the rules for requesting a salary",
            "Build your CV in the SNSF portal CV tool to get the required format and net academic age",
            "Prepare a research plan and declare any ethical implications"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Missing the 5 May 2026 17:00 CEST deadline",
            "Not having the host confirmation letter signed, which blocks the submission",
            "Falling outside the eligibility window",
            "Already having achieved the objective of the call by leading a 2-3 person group or holding significant funding",
            "Holding an individual SNSF Project Funding grant or an approved/ongoing PRIMA, Eccellenza, SNSF StG, ERC StG or Practice-to Science",
