          "description": "The France Excellence Eiffel scholarship is a French Ministry of Foreign Affairs programme managed by Campus France that funds tuition fees plus a monthly allowance for students from non-European Economic Area countries studying in France at under 25 (master's) or under 30 (doctoral). Candidates are selected and nominated by French institutions, which build a master list of excellence of up to three candidates per scheme and discipline. Campus France makes the payments, and the scheme does not cover housing, health insurance or transport.",
