          "description": "The TulÄ« Takes Flight scholarship is part of the New Zealand government's gesture of goodwill and reconciliation to Aotearoa Pacific communities following the 2021 apology for the Dawn Raids, and is designed to reduce financial barriers to study or training in Aotearoa. It funds full-time vocational or academic study from NZQA level 4 up to doctoral level, at NZD 12,500 per year for vocational and undergraduate study and NZD 17,500 per year for postgraduate study, for one, two or three years. It is restricted to New Zealand citizens and permanent residents of indigenous Pacific cultural heritage who have lived in New Zealand for the last three years.",
          "program_type": "Government scholarship funded by the Ministry of Education and administered by the Pacific Education Foundation",
          "region": "New Zealand",
          "coverage": "Provides a capped annual award of NZD 12,500 or NZD 17,500 that can cover full-time course costs including tuition fees, equipment and materials, and can help with accommodation, transport and childcare; the page does not state that all costs of study are met.",
