          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "Scholarships are organised by college: College of Business, Public Policy and Law; Shannon College of Hotel Management; College of Science and Engineering; College of Arts, Social Sciences and Celtic Studies; and College of Medicine and Health. Government of Ireland Education Scholarships are restricted to a named list of eligible programmes across those colleges. The CSC joint PhD scholarship has no subject restrictions.",
          "application_method": "The Global Scholarships hub directs applicants to the college-specific scholarship pages and to the standard University of Galway application process. For the CSC joint PhD scholarship, the process is: find a supervisor via FindaSupervisor, agree a project plan using the CSC 2026 application form, have the supervisor email the Research Plan Template to the relevant college by 27 February 2026, await a conditional college offer by 13 March 2026, translate the research plan into Chinese, then apply through the CSC portal at apply.csc.edu.cn.",
