          },
          "description": "Entrusted by the Ministry of Education of the People's Republic of China, the University of Chinese Academy of Sciences recruits outstanding young graduate students from around the world and provides full scholarships through the 2026 Chinese Government Scholarship call. Successful Master's students are exempted from RMB 30,000/year tuition and successful PhD students from RMB 40,000/year, receive monthly stipends of RMB 3,500 and RMB 5,000 respectively, free UCAS Beijing campus accommodation or a housing subsidy of up to RMB 700-1,000/month, and RMB 800 medical insurance, for 36 months. Applicants must be non-Chinese citizens, hold an equivalent degree, be within the age limits of 35 (Master's) or 40 (PhD), be proficient in English or Mandarin, and submit the same information to both the CSC Online Application System (UCAS agency number 80001) and UCAS's own admission system by 31 January 2026 Beijing Time.",
