            "Must remain in good standing with OSAP for the entirety of the award period, and must not have defaulted on student loans or have an overpayment",
            "Must immediately inform both the graduate unit and the Graduate Awards Office of any change to registration status, temporary or permanent, during the award",
            "Must maintain accurate and current mailing and direct deposit information on ACORN",
            "Award offers must be accepted by completing an SGS Award Payment Activation form through the SGS Forms Tool",
            "May accept research assistantships, part-time teaching positions or other paid employment that does not affect full-time status and is commensurate with graduate unit policies; students in full-time paid employment are typically ineligible",
            "Cannot hold an OGS in the same session or the same award year as a scholarship from SSHRC, NSERC, CIHR, QEII-GSST, or another OGS",
            "Award holders who opt to apply for OSAP assistance should not report their OGS or QEII-GSST funding to OSAP, as SGS reports this on their behalf, and must report any other awards or fellowship funding",
            "Recipients who are enrolled in a postgraduate MD training program and simultaneously registered in a full-time doctoral graduate program may hold other awards that, together with the OGS, do not exceed the current level of funding for clinical training provided by the Ontario Ministry of Health"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "SGS Inclusive Excellence Graduate Scholarship competition: OGS awards valued at up to $15,000 per year and other SGS awards valued at $10,000 per year are made available to Black and Indigenous scholars, with approximately 25 awards available annually. No separate application is required; eligible OGS applicants who identify as Black and/or Indigenous to Canada and who have not received an OGS offer by the time of the SGS competition are automatically considered, with offers issued by 31 July.",
            "The Queen Elizabeth II Graduate Scholarship in Science and Technology (QEII-GSST, formerly OGSST) is a related award governed by the same guide, with a separate contact",
            "Start dates may be chosen as May or September of the awarding year, or January of the following calendar year, subject to continuing to meet all terms and conditions",
            "Start dates may be deferred for up to 4 sessions (16 months) from September of the awarding year for eligible reasons and with graduate unit approval, without affecting award value or duration",
            "An award may be interrupted after a minimum of one session for a leave of absence, with the award end date extended by the leave duration, for relevant work experience, parental or family-related responsibilities, or medical reasons, with documentation required",
            "Fundraising acknowledgement letters are not required for donors in the Faculty of Arts & Science; other faculties have named advancement contacts"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "Debbie Chau, Graduate Awards Officer, Graduate Awards Office, School of Graduate Studies, ogs@utoronto.ca, 416-978-2382. Contact for QEII-GSST: debbie.chau@utoronto.ca. Questions on the OGS competition or nomination process go to your graduate unit."
          },
          "description": "The Ontario Graduate Scholarship encourages excellence in graduate studies at publicly-assisted universities in Ontario, and the U of T program is jointly funded by the Province of Ontario and the University of Toronto, which is allocated a fixed number of awards annually. The award is worth $5,000 per session, so $10,000 for two consecutive sessions or $15,000 for three, with the awarding graduate unit contributing one third of the total, and is tenable for one year. Applicants need an A- or equivalent in each of the last two completed years, must be registered full-time in an eligible two- or three-term programme, and are assessed on relevant experience and achievements (up to 40%), plan of study (up to 30%) and two academic assessment reports (up to 30%). Canadian citizens, permanent residents and protected persons qualify, and international students on valid study permits compete for a set number of awards through a centralized adjudication of graduate unit nominations, with results in mid-July.",
          "program_type": "Government-funded merit-based graduate scholarship (province-university funded) with a centralized university adjudication",
          "region": "Canada (Ontario, University of Toronto)",
          "coverage": "A value-based scholarship of $5,000 per session for two or three sessions ($10,000 or $15,000 per year), with the graduate unit contributing one third of the cost; it is not described as a tuition waiver, and any funds left after tuition charges are refunded.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Identify the exact internal deadline set by each graduate unit you are targeting, since that is the only operative application date",
            "Submit a separate OGS application to every graduate unit you apply to, because awards are not transferable between units",
            "If you are an international student, make sure your study permit is valid and effective by your graduate unit's OGS international application deadline",
            "Confirm you hold at least an A- (or equivalent) in each of the last two completed years, or an overall A- on graduate courses if you have two or more years of graduate study",
            "Have at least 60% of a full course load registered to count as full-time, or 40% with a permanent disability",
            "Check you have not exhausted the lifetime maximum of government-funded support: 2 years of OGS/QEII-GSST for master's, 4 years for doctoral, 6 years combined",
            "Prepare the plan of study to a strict 2-page limit: 1 page of plan and 1 page of references",
            "Secure two academic referees who will submit their letters online, and brief them on the criteria that carry the 15% each",
            "Make sure you are in good standing with OSAP, and clear any restriction within 30 days of notification if awarded",
            "Note that the award is paid through ACORN, so set up direct deposit before accepting"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Missing the graduate unit's internal deadline, since there is no central deadline and the unit's date is the only one that counts",
            "Submitting one application and expecting it to cover several graduate units, as awards are not transferable between units or universities",
            "Missing the plan of study page limit, which makes the application incomplete",
            "Not holding a valid study permit by the graduate unit's OGS international application deadline as an international applicant",
            "Falling below the A- threshold in either of the last two completed years",
            "Holding an overlapping SSHRC, NSERC, CIHR, QEII-GSST or another OGS award in the same session or award year",
            "Defaulting on a Canada or Ontario student loan, which makes an applicant ineligible even if otherwise qualified",
            "Taking full-time paid employment, which typically makes a student ineligible",
            "Overlooking that January and May instalments go against tuition and charges first, with only the remainder refunded"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Tuition fees beyond the portion of the award that offsets them through ACORN",
            "Living costs, since the award is $10,000 or $15,000 per year and not a full cost-of-attendance package",
            "Health insurance and incidental fees not covered by the award",
            "A second year of funding after the maximum is reached, which is 2 years for master's and 4 for doctoral",
            "Books, materials, conference travel and research costs"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Verify the OGS application form, transcripts, prior awards/publications/conference/research experience, plan of study and both references are all present, since all components are online and the application is incomplete without them",
            "Confirm the plan of study PDF is within 2 pages with 1 page for the plan and 1 page for references",
            "Check that both referees have actually submitted, since referees must submit online",
            "Keep your study permit validity date visible against the graduate unit's international deadline",
            "After award, complete the SGS Award Payment Activation form and set up ACORN direct deposit"
          ],
          "alerts": [
            {
              "trigger": "You are an international student on a study permit",
              "message": "You compete for a set number of OGS awards, are nominated by your graduate unit to a centralized adjudication, and must hold a valid permit by the unit's OGS international deadline. Awards cannot be transferred between units."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "You are Black and/or Indigenous to Canada",
              "message": "Identify yourself on the OGS application and, if you have no OGS offer by the time of the SGS competition, you are automatically considered for OGS awards up to $15,000 per year and other SGS awards of $10,000 per year, with approximately 25 awards annually. Offers are issued by 31 July."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "You withdraw, transfer to part-time, or complete your degree early",
              "message": "You must repay the funds received for the incomplete session, and awards terminated by early completion are prorated to the new end date."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "You are already on OSAP",
              "message": "Do not report your OGS or QEII-GSST funding to OSAP; SGS reports it for you. But other awards or fellowships you receive must be reported, and OGS counts as a resource that can reduce OSAP."
            }
          ],
          "submission_workflow": [
            "Check your status eligibility: Canadian citizen, permanent resident or protected person, or a valid study permit by the unit's international deadline",
            "Confirm your GPA meets the A- threshold and that you are within the lifetime support maximums",
            "List every graduate unit you are applying to and find each unit's internal OGS deadline",
            "Register full-time in an eligible two- or three-term programme",
            "Prepare the online OGS application: form, transcripts, prior awards and research experience, a 2-page plan of study, and two online academic references",
            "Submit the application separately to each graduate unit by that unit's deadline",
            "If shortlisted, your unit nominates you to SGS for centralized adjudication; results are published mid-July",
            "If awarded, clear any OSAP restriction within 30 days, complete the SGS Award Payment Activation form, set up ACORN direct deposit, and confirm the full-time registration for all sessions"
          ]
        },
        "programme_verification": {
          "cycle_verified": "2026-2027 registration year with mid-July results; all application dates set by individual graduate units, and no updated dates for a subsequent cycle are published on the page",
          "verification_confidence": 0.87,
          "official_fields_confirmed": [
            "value: $5,000 per session; $10,000 for two consecutive sessions or $15,000 for three consecutive sessions",
            "awarding graduate unit contributes one third of the total cost",
            "jointly funded by the Province of Ontario and the University of Toronto, with a provincial allocation per university",
            "tenable for one year, two or three consecutive academic sessions, each session four months",
            "eligibility: Canadian citizen/PR/protected person by the unit deadline, or international student on a valid study permit for a set number of awards; full-time registration in an eligible two- or three-term programme in 2026-2027; not exceeded lifetime maximum; at least A- in each of the last two completed years",
            "full-time defined as at least 60% of a full course load, 40% for students with a permanent disability",
            "selection weighting: relevant experience and achievements up to 40%, plan of study up to 30%, academic assessment reports up to 30% at 15% each",
            "document list: OGS form, transcripts (unofficial permitted), prior awards/publications/conference/research experience, 2-page plan of study, two online academic references",
            "deadlines are set by each graduate unit; results mid-July; nominations forwarded to SGS per the SGS Memo",
            "awards are not transferable between universities or between U of T graduate units",
            "maximum support: 2 years master's, 4 years doctoral, 6 years lifetime combined with listed government programs",
