          "deadline_note": "The deadline is set by the Department of Foreign Affairs, Trade and Development (DFATD) for Canadian institutions to submit applications on behalf of candidates; it is not a student-facing deadline. The page states Canadian institutions should establish an earlier deadline with candidates and their home institutions to ensure timely receipt of supporting documents.",
          "status": "CLOSED",
          "status_note": "The page states the application period for 2025 is closed, and that only applications for Fall 2025 were accepted, with selected candidates arriving between August 1 and October 1, 2025. The page notes the 2025 application deadline of 11:59 p.m. EDT, March 31, 2025, and no later cycle is published.",
          "funding_amount": 10200,
          "funding_currency": "CAD",
          "funding_period": "one-off",
          "funding_duration": "Four months or one academic term",
          "tuition_coverage": true,
          "tuition_coverage_note": "The page states a valid student exchange agreement that waives tuition fees for scholarship recipients is required for college and undergraduate study, and that a student exchange agreement is not required for graduate study. Canadian post-secondary institutions must have a valid student exchange agreement with the student's home institution that waives tuition fees, required for college/undergraduate study only. The scholarship value of 10,200 CAD is for college/undergraduate and graduate study, and selected candidates may use the funds towards listed eligible expenses.",
          "living_cost_coverage": true,
          "travel_coverage": true,
          "fully_funded": true,
          "funding_label": "SEED-2 scholarship (10,200 CAD)",
          "benefits": [
            "Scholarship value of 10,200 CAD for college/undergraduate study and for graduate study",
            "Duration of four months or one academic term",
            "Selected candidates may use the scholarship funds towards visa or study/work permit fees, airfare via the most direct and economical route, health insurance, living expenses such as accommodation, utilities and food, ground transportation including a public transportation pass, and books and supplies required for study or research (excluding computers and other equipment)",
            "Canadian institutions are eligible to receive 500 CAD per scholarship recipient to aid with administrative costs once the student arrives in Canada, and reimbursement of additional employer compliance fees paid to Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada in some cases",
            "Scholarships are not taxable for either the Canadian institution or the scholarship recipient"
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Candidates must be citizens of an ASEAN member state: Brunei Darussalam, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos (Lao People's Democratic Republic), Malaysia, Myanmar, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, or Vietnam",
            "Candidates must be enrolled full-time at a post-secondary institution in an ASEAN member state",
            "Candidates must be paying tuition fees to that institution at the time of application and for the full duration of their exchange",
            "Candidates must not hold or have a pending application for Canadian citizenship or permanent residency",
            "Candidates must not already be participating in a scholarship program funded by the Government of Canada",
            "Candidates must not already be enrolled in a degree, diploma or certificate program at a Canadian post-secondary institution",
            "Candidates must not have previously received a scholarship under the SEED program",
            "Canadian host institutions must be a Designated Learning Institution (DLI), have a valid student exchange agreement with the student's home institution that waives tuition fees (required for college/undergraduate study only), and centralize all applications through their international office"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Candidates must be citizens of an ASEAN member state and be enrolled full-time at a post-secondary institution in an ASEAN member state, paying tuition fees. Candidates who hold or have a pending application for Canadian citizenship or permanent residency are not eligible.",
          "international_eligibility": "Explicit: open to citizens of ASEAN member states enrolled full-time at an ASEAN post-secondary institution. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are excluded.",
          "degree_levels": [
            "Undergraduate",
            "Master's",
            "PhD"
          ],
          "study_mode": "full-time",
          "research_requirement": "not stated",
          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "The proposed study or research in Canada must contribute to the implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development and the achievement of all Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",
          "application_method": "Canadian post-secondary institutions must apply on behalf of eligible candidates through the My EduCanada online system. The institution assigns a program coordinator, creates a My EduCanada Institution account, selects the Canada-ASEAN Scholarships and Educational Exchanges for Development Program, enters the required data, uploads supporting documents, reviews the application, reads and accepts the conditions of the Declaration and permission statement, and submits. Students wishing to pursue short-term studies or research in Canada should review the eligibility criteria and contact their institution's international office for application details.",
          "application_route": "university nomination",
          "requirements": [
            "Be a citizen of an ASEAN member state",
            "Be enrolled full-time at a post-secondary institution in an ASEAN member state",
            "Be paying tuition fees to that institution at the time of application and for the full duration of the exchange",
            "Not hold or have a pending application for Canadian citizenship or permanent residency",
            "Not be participating in another Government of Canada funded scholarship program",
            "Not already be enrolled in a degree, diploma or certificate program at a Canadian post-secondary institution",
            "Not have previously received a SEED scholarship"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "Proof of citizenship: a copy of the candidate's passport or national identity card with a photo and valid dates, from the same country as the citizenship selected in the online application form",
            "Signed Privacy Notice Statement for non-Canadian participants, signed by the candidate and dated within the last six months",
            "Letter of intent from the candidate, maximum one page, explaining the nature of studies or research, the rationale for study in Canada, and how the proposed study relates to the 2030 Agenda and identifies the Sustainable Development Goal",
            "Letter of proof of full-time enrolment from the home institution, on official letterhead, dated within the last six months, confirming current full-time enrolment (transcripts, a student card, or a letter of admission are not acceptable)",
            "Letter of support from the home institution, maximum one page, on official letterhead, dated within the last six months, from the candidate's instructor, professor or international director",
            "Letter of invitation from the Canadian supervisor (graduate students only), maximum one page, on institutional letterhead, dated within the last six months, confirming willingness to support and mentor the candidate, and confirming that tuition fees are waived when there is no MOU in force",
            "Signed copy of the Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) or Agreement with the partner institution indicating that tuition fees will not be charged, for college and undergraduate research applications; expired agreements will not be accepted",
            "A ranking of applications, based on the institution's strategic priorities, indicating the MyEduCanada application number of each candidate, sent to seed-bpeed@cbie.ca",
            "Documents in a language other than English or French must be accompanied by a translation, and each document must be smaller than 5 MB and in .jpg, .gif, .png, .pdf, .doc, .docx, .txt or .xlsx format"
          ],
          "english_requirement": null,
          "english_requirement_note": "The SEED page does not publish an English language proficiency requirement. It does state that documents in a language other than English or French must be accompanied by a translation, but this is a document requirement, not a test score requirement.",
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Applications are evaluated based on the linkage of the proposed research or study to the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development",
            "The candidate's commitment to use their proposed research or studies in Canada to help combat poverty and narrow the development gap in the ASEAN region",
            "The merit of the research or study to be undertaken in Canada",
            "The benefit to the home institution and peers",
            "The benefit to the Canadian institution, supervisor and peers",
            "The strength of the linkages to be created through the proposed exchange",
            "The rankings submitted by the Canadian institution, based on the institution's strategic priorities"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": "Rankings submitted by the Canadian institution, based on the institution's strategic priorities, are a stated selection factor and must indicate the MyEduCanada application number of each candidate.",
          "duration": "Four months or one academic term, for both college/undergraduate and graduate study.",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "Scholarship recipients must engage in full-time studies or research as defined by the Canadian institution",
            "Recipients must abstain from clinical training or clinically-oriented research involving direct patient care",
            "Recipients must focus primarily on full-time studies or research during their stay in Canada",
            "Recipients must return to their home institutions after the scholarship period to complete their studies",
            "Failure to meet these conditions may result in the cancellation of the scholarship",
            "Selected candidates may arrive in Canada as early as August 1, 2025 and no later than October 1, 2025, for the 2025 cycle",
            "Scholarships cannot be deferred and are not renewable",
            "Scholarships are subject to availability of funding from the Government of Canada",
            "If a selected candidate does not take up the scholarship, the Canadian institution must return the funds, including the administrative fee, to DFATD"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "Canadian institutions may receive 500 CAD per scholarship recipient to aid with administrative costs once the student arrives in Canada",
            "Canadian institutions may be eligible for reimbursement of additional employer compliance fees paid to Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada in some cases",
            "Scholarships are not taxable for either the Canadian institution or the scholarship recipient"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "seed-bpeed@international.gc.ca",
            "seed_program_team": "seed-bpeed@cbie.ca"
          },
          "description": "The Canada-ASEAN Scholarships and Educational Exchanges for Development (SEED) program is a short-term exchange offered by Global Affairs Canada, enabling students from ASEAN member states to conduct study or research at a Canadian post-secondary institution in areas that contribute to the implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development. It provides 10,200 CAD for four months or one academic term, funding eligible expenses including airfare, health insurance, living expenses, ground transportation and books. Canadian institutions apply on behalf of candidates through My EduCanada, and the 2025 application period is closed.",
          "program_type": "Government-to-government scholarship (exchange)",
          "region": "North America (Canada)",
          "coverage": "Covers 10,200 CAD for four months or one academic term, applicable to visa or permit fees, airfare, health insurance, living expenses, ground transportation, and books and supplies; college and undergraduate tuition fees are waived through a required student exchange agreement, and graduate study does not require an agreement.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you are a citizen of an ASEAN member state and are enrolled full-time at a post-secondary institution in an ASEAN member state paying tuition fees",
