            "Not published in the Fudan notice. Selection is carried out by the China Scholarship Council and Fudan University, and the document publishes no criteria or weighting."
          ],
          "selection_weighting": null,
          "duration": "Duration follows the degree programme studied; no fixed number of years is stated in the Fudan notice",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "New scholarship students are required to register at Fudan University on the dates specified on the admission notice; students who arrive late without approval in advance will have their scholarship automatically cancelled",
            "New scholarship students must participate in annual evaluation; those who fail to meet the requirements will have their scholarship cancelled",
            "New scholarship students are not allowed to change the major or the study period",
            "Scholarships awarded by the Chinese government shall not be subsidised by other scholarships (excluding all kinds of one-time awards) established by the Chinese government at all levels and the admitted university at the same time; once found, the Chinese Government Scholarship qualification will be cancelled and the scholarship received should be returned",
            "Those who deliberately conceal their financial support are not allowed to apply for Chinese Government Scholarships within three years, besides disqualification"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "Results are checked by visiting the \"Notices\" column on the Fudan International Students Office website (https://iso.fudan.edu.cn/isoenglish/)"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "Fudan University International Students Office, 220 Handan Road, Yangpu District, Shanghai 200433 (page publisher: Zhang Xiangrong; notice published 2025-10-31)"
          },
          "description": "Fudan University's notice for the 2026 Chinese Government Scholarship under the University Program (also titled Chinese University Program on the webpage) covers master's and doctoral applicants who are non-Chinese citizens in good health, under 35 for master's and under 40 for doctoral study. The award exempts tuition, provides free on-campus accommodation or an accommodation subsidy, comprehensive medical insurance, and a living stipend of RMB 3,000 per month for master's and RMB 3,500 for doctoral students. Applications are made in two stages: online at www.campuschina.org under Program Category Type B with Fudan agency number 10246, then through the Fudan istudent application system with fund source set to \"Self-support\" and the scholarship application form uploaded.",
          "program_type": "Government-funded full scholarship administered by a host university (national scholarship, Type B / university program)",
          "region": "China (Shanghai)",
          "coverage": "Covers tuition exemption, on-campus accommodation or an accommodation subsidy, comprehensive medical insurance, and a monthly living stipend of RMB 3,000 (master's) or RMB 3,500 (doctoral); the notice does not mention travel or airfare support.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you are a non-Chinese citizen in good health and under 35 (master's) or under 40 (doctoral)",
            "Register at www.campuschina.org with Program Category Type B and Fudan University Agency No. 10246, then print and sign the form",
            "Complete the Fudan istudent application at https://istudent.fudan.edu.cn/apply with fund source \"Self-support\"",
            "Select \"Chinese Government Scholarship\" in the Fudan form and upload the signed CSC application form",
            "Book and complete the Foreigner Physical Examination Form early - it is only valid for six months, so timing it near submission is risky but booking late is worse",
            "If you already reside in China, confirm you can supply a Residence Permit or Foreign Permanent Resident ID Card instead of the medical examination form",
            "Check you are not holding any other Chinese government scholarship, since holding one disqualifies you"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Selecting more than one school, since Category B applicants can only choose one",
            "Failing to select \"Fudan University\" in the CSC system while using Fudan's agency number",
            "Forgetting to set the fund source to \"Self-support\" in the Fudan system, which is the Fudan-specific instruction",
            "Uploading an incomplete or expired Foreigner Physical Examination Form",
            "Exceeding the age caps of 35 for master's or 40 for doctoral study",
            "Holding another Chinese government scholarship, which is disqualifying",
            "Applying after 10 December 2025 for the 2026 intake"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Airfare and international travel, which the notice does not list among the covered items",
            "Books, materials and laboratory or project costs, which are not mentioned",
            "Living costs beyond the monthly stipend, including any shortfall between the RMB 3,000/RMB 3,500 stipend and actual local costs",
            "Costs arising after any change of study period, which the terms prohibit"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Verify the Foreigner Physical Examination Form covers all required items, is signed by the attending physician and stamped by the hospital, and is within its six-month validity",
            "Confirm the signed CSC form is legible and matches the data in both online systems",
            "Check that the agency number on the CSC form is exactly 10246 for Fudan University",
            "Retain evidence of any other funding you hold, to demonstrate you are not in breach of the single-scholarship rule"
          ],
          "alerts": [
            {
              "trigger": "The 10 December 2025 deadline passes",
              "message": "The 2026 cycle is closed. Use the result check route instead: the \"Notices\" column on iso.fudan.edu.cn/isoenglish/ publishes the outcome."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "You are offered another Chinese government or admitted-university scholarship",
              "message": "Holding both cancels the Chinese Government Scholarship and requires the funds to be returned; deliberate concealment also bars you for three years."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "The admission notice specifies registration dates",
              "message": "Arriving late without prior approval automatically cancels the scholarship, so plan travel around the registration date rather than the start of teaching."
            }
          ],
          "submission_workflow": [
            "Verify nationality, health and age eligibility",
            "Apply at www.campuschina.org using Program Category Type B, Agency No. 10246, and print and sign the form",
            "Complete the Foreigner Physical Examination Form in Chinese or English within its six-month validity window",
            "Apply through the Fudan istudent system, choosing \"Self-support\" as fund source",
            "In the Fudan form choose \"Chinese Government Scholarship\" and upload the signed CSC application form and the medical examination form",
            "Submit before 10 December 2025 and monitor the \"Notices\" column on the ISO website for the result"
          ]
        },
        "programme_verification": {
