          "description": "The UNESCO/Poland Co-Sponsored Fellowships Programme in Engineering places 28 fellowships at the UNESCO Chair for Science, Technology and Engineering at AGH University of Krakow at the disposal of developing Member States, for a 6-month individual research programme between 1 October 2025 and 31 March 2026. The Polish authorities provide free tuition, a monthly allowance of 1,800 PLN for BSc and 2,200 PLN for MSc students and a one-time special allowance, while UNESCO covers international travel, health insurance and a USD 120 pocket allowance. Applications are only accepted through the applicant's National Commission for UNESCO.",
