          "description": "The Lee Kuan Yew Scholarship, set up in 1991 by the Tanjong Pagar Citizens' Consultative Committee with public funding, is Singapore's premier postgraduate scholarship and is open to Singapore citizens. Recipients receive full tuition fees coverage and an annual allowance of S$50,000 for up to 2 years for a Master's degree or up to 5 years for PhD studies, with no restrictions on the course of study and no bond, though recipients are expected to contribute to Singapore society. Applications are submitted through the PSC Gateway portal with a published deadline of 28 February, and the page states applications for the 2026 award are closed.",
