        "description": "Australia Awards Fellowships is a DFAT competitive grants programme that funds Australian Host Organisations to bring mid-career and senior officials from ODA-eligible developing countries to Australia for 2-52 week short-term professional development placements, typically in Australia followed by in-partner country implementation activities. Funding of up to AUD 34,500 per Fellow is offered competitively and the Australian Host Organisation must provide a co-contribution. Individuals cannot apply; a host organisation in Australia submits on the Fellow's behalf. Round 21 closed on 16 January 2026 and Round 22 is expected to open in the final quarter of 2026.",
