          "funding_label": "Up to AUD 34,500 per Fellow, competitively awarded, with a mandatory Australian Host Organisation co-contribution",
          "benefits": [
            "Funding of up to $34,500 per Fellow, offered on a competitive basis",
            "Access to high-quality training, exchange of expertise, skills and knowledge, and networking",
            "Activities may combine short-term study and/or training, research, professional attachments and networking",
            "DFAT funds and provides visa support letters for individual Fellows"
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Australian Organisations in partnership with Overseas Counterpart Organisations (OCOs) in eligible developing countries are eligible to apply. 'Individuals cannot apply.'",
            "Applicants must be Australian Organisations who are legal entities with a current Australian Business Number (ABN). Examples given include private sector, research centres, higher education providers, VET providers, peak bodies, chambers of commerce, community groups, NGOs, media organisations, professional associations and industry bodies, plus Australian Government departments, agencies, statutory authorities and Government Business Enterprises",
            "Australian Organisations must demonstrate links with OCOs in eligible countries and commit through an in-kind and/or financial co-contribution",
            "OCOs cannot be an international arm or branch of the Australian Organisation, nor under the same overarching international organisation or consortium; OCOs must operate and reside in an eligible country and cannot be individuals",
            "New or emerging partnerships with OCOs will be considered",
            "Fellows must be a minimum of 18 years of age at the time of commencing the Fellowship",
            "Fellows must not be an Australian citizen or be applying for Australian citizenship, including dual citizenship where one citizenship is Australian",
            "Fellows must not have Australian permanent resident status or be applying for Australian permanent residency",
            "Fellows must be a citizen of and residing in an eligible developing country; country of citizenship and residency may differ",
            "Fellows must not be current serving military personnel",
            "Fellows must not be married or engaged to, or be a de facto of, a person who holds or is eligible to hold Australian or New Zealand citizenship or permanent residency",
            "Fellows must have been working in their country of citizenship or residency, in an area relevant to the Fellowship activities, preceding the proposed commencement date",
            "Fellows must be able to satisfy all requirements determined by the Department of Home Affairs for a visa",
            "Fellows must be able to participate for the full proposed duration, except in exceptional circumstances approved by the Australia Awards Global Support Unit and DFAT",
            "Fellows must be able to travel without family members"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Individual Fellows must be citizens of and residing in an eligible developing country, and must not hold or be applying for Australian citizenship or permanent residency. Applying entities must be Australian Organisations holding a current ABN, partnered with an OCO resident in an eligible country.",
          "international_eligibility": "Explicit - the programme is a people-to-people exchange placing participants FROM ODA-eligible developing countries INTO Australian organisations, with a closed list of eligible countries by region (Pacific, Southeast Asia, South Asia and Middle East, Africa, Caribbean, and Ukraine in Europe).",
          "degree_levels": [
            "Not a degree programme - short-term professional development / non-degree training, research, professional attachment or networking"
          ],
          "study_mode": "not stated",
          "research_requirement": "not required",
          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "Fellowship programmes must align with one of six development priority areas: (1) Climate change, adaptation, resilience and green energy transition including critical mineral mining; (2) Health; (3) Gender equality, disability equity and social inclusion; (4) Digital Economy, cyber resilience, and media engagement; (5) Maritime and the Blue Economy; (6) Infrastructure and connectivity.",
          "application_method": "The Australian Host Organisation submits the application, not the individual Fellow. Applications are prepared against the Call for proposals and Guide for Applicants, then submitted through the online system, which may include registering the project application, granting partner access, uploading required annexes using the Letter of Intent, Work Programme and External Consultant templates, and signing and submitting the application electronically with a qualified certificate for electronic signature. A legal representative of the applicant institution, or a person duly authorised by them, must sign. No direct application URL is published on the pages read; resources are published as round-specific documents.",
          "application_route": "agency-specific",
          "requirements": [
            "An eligible Australian Host Organisation with a current ABN submits the application",
            "A named OCO resident in an eligible country that is not an arm, branch or sibling of the Australian Organisation",
            "The proposal must align with one of the six development priority areas",
            "The Australian Organisation must provide an in-kind and/or financial co-contribution",
            "The application must include in-partner country activity",
            "A minimum of two weeks must be delivered in Australia",
            "The Fellowship must be between 2 and 52 weeks in total, inclusive of in-Australia, online and in-partner country activities",
            "In-Australia activity duration must be longer than the in-partner country activity duration",
            "The Applicant Organisation must not have exceeded six applications",
            "The application must not exceed 15 DFAT-funded Fellows (excluding AHO/OCO funded Fellows)",
            "The submitting officer must be an employee of the Australian Organisation",
            "The Applicant must not be listed in the National Redress Scheme, the Anticorruption and Integrity Sanctions list, the World Bank Listing of Ineligible Firms and Individuals, terrorist organisations lists, or the Consolidated List"
          ],
          "documents": [
