          "english_requirement": null,
          "english_requirement_note": "DFAT requires only that a Fellow 'have an adequate level of English language ability to be able to fully participate in the program, including an ability to complete the Fellow's Completion Survey at the conclusion of their Fellowship.' No test, score or level is published. The Australian Host Organisation is responsible for ensuring adequate English or for implementing appropriate measures such as translation services, and DFAT does not recommend translation services for Multi-country Fellowships where they may compromise learning outcomes or where Fellows' English levels differ substantially.",
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Alignment with one of the six development priority areas",
            "Demonstrated links with an OCO in an eligible country and commitment through in-kind and/or financial co-contribution",
            "Compliance with all mandatory application compliance criteria, which applications MUST meet to progress to assessment",
            "At least two weeks delivered in Australia, and in-Australia duration longer than in-partner country duration",
            "A proposal that builds the capacity of mid-career and senior officials positioned to lead priority development and foreign affairs outcomes",
            "A proposal that develops and strengthens institutional partnerships and people-to-people links between Australian and overseas counterpart organisations"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": null,
          "duration": "Australia Awards Fellowships range between 2-52 weeks, commencing in Australia, followed by in-partner country activities focused on implementation and exchange of expertise, skills and knowledge. The duration of in-partner country activities must not exceed the duration of activities in Australia.",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "DFAT only funds and provides visa support letters for individual Fellows, not their family members, and Fellows must be able to travel without family",
