            "website": "Australia Awards",
            "department": "Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade, R.G. Casey Building, John McEwen Crescent, Barton ACT 0221 Australia, Phone: +61 2 6261 1111, ABN: 47 065 634 525"
          },
          "description": "Australia Awards Fellowships is a DFAT competitive grants programme that funds Australian Host Organisations to bring mid-career and senior officials from ODA-eligible developing countries to Australia for 2-52 week short-term professional development placements, typically in Australia followed by in-partner country implementation activities. Funding of up to AUD 34,500 per Fellow is offered competitively and the Australian Host Organisation must provide a co-contribution. Individuals cannot apply; a host organisation in Australia submits on the Fellow's behalf. Round 21 closed on 16 January 2026 and Round 22 is expected to open in the final quarter of 2026.",
          "program_type": "Government-funded short-term professional development and people-to-people grants programme (not a degree scholarship)",
          "region": "Australia, with in-partner country components in ODA-eligible developing countries",
          "coverage": "Provides up to AUD 34,500 per Fellow for a 2-52 week placement covering a combination of short-term study, training, research, professional attachments and networking, plus visa support for the individual Fellow only; it is not described as covering tuition, and the mandatory host co-contribution and family-exclusion rules mean it is not a full personal funding package.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Identify an Australian Host Organisation willing to apply for you - you cannot apply yourself, and the ABN requirement is absolute",
            "Confirm your country appears on the eligible list for your region; Ukraine is the only European entry",
            "Check you are not Australian (or NZ-linked through a spouse/partner) and hold no Australian permanent residency or application for it",
            "Confirm you have worked in your country of citizenship or residency in an area relevant to the Fellowship before the proposed start date",
            "Align the proposed activities with one of the six named priority areas - this is a mandatory compliance criterion",
            "Be ready to travel without family and to complete the Fellowship's Completion Survey",
            "Read the Round guidelines DOCX/PDF and the FAQ before the host organisation drafts the application"
