        "eligibility": [
          "Be a citizen of a country other than the People's Republic of China, and be in good health both mentally and physically",
          "Be a high school graduate under the age of 25 when applying for undergraduate programs",
          "Be a bachelor's degree holder under the age of 35 when applying for master's programs",
          "Be a master's degree holder under the age of 40 when applying for doctoral programs",
          "Be a high school graduate (at least) under the age of 45 when applying for general scholar programs",
          "Be a master's degree holder or an associate professor (or above) under the age of 50 when applying for senior scholar programs",
          "Take the China Scholastic Competency Assessment (CSCA) and upload a valid score report when applying for bachelor programs",
          "Have acquired HSK Level 3 when applying for Chinese-taught general scholar programs (those studying Chinese are exempted)",
          "Have acquired HSK Level 3 when applying for Chinese-taught senior scholar programs",
          "Have acquired HSK Level 4 when applying for Chinese-taught master's or doctoral programs",
          "Applicants who obtained their degree from a Chinese university using Chinese as the teaching language do not need to provide relevant language proficiency certificates",
          "Meet the admission requirements of the applied universities in terms of academic ability, language proficiency and other relevant criteria"
        ],
        "eligibility_summary": "Indonesian citizens (non-PRC), in good mental and physical health, not Chinese citizens. China-Indonesia Scholarship in Higher Education Program. Must meet admission requirements of target universities. Applicants for English-taught programs must provide IELTS/TOEFL scores.",
        "benefits": [
          "Full scholarship, stated as a China - Indonesia Scholarship in Higher Education Program",
          "20 places for undergraduate, master's and doctoral programs",
          "Recruiting students who go to China to study marine, medical, health, tourism, education and other required majors",
          "Tuition, and living costs as part of the full scholarship description",
          "Excludes international travel expenses, which the applicant must fund"
        ],
        "coverage": "Described as a full scholarship covering tuition and living costs for study in China, but explicitly excluding international travel expenses, which the applicant must meet.",
        "requirements": [
          "Submit the online application and all documents in the system before February 8, 2026",
          "Use Indonesian Agency Number 3602",
          "Obtain at least one pre-admission document from the universities applied for, such as a pre-admission notice from the international students' admission department or an invitation letter from a school or professor",
          "For bachelor's applicants, register for and take the CSCA before the application deadline and obtain a valid score report; those intending to enrol in September 2026 must register for and take the CSCA on December 21, 2025, or January 25, 2026",
          "Provide notarized Chinese or English translations of any documents not in Chinese or English",
          "Meet the admission requirements of the applied university in academic ability and language proficiency"
        ],
        "documents": [
          "\">b) Passport Home Page: Applicants are required to submit a clear scanned copy of the information page of their ordinary passports",
          "An applicant who fails to apply for a passport due to objective reasons may submit valid documentation or documentary evidence that carries information about the full English name",
          "such as IELTS or TOEFL score reports",
          "\">i) Recommendation letters: Applicants for graduate programs or senior scholar programs must submit two letters of recommendation in Chinese or English from professors or associate professors.</span></p><p style=\"margin-right: 0px"
        ],
        "english_requirement": "Edition of Xi Jinping: The Governance of China (Volume V) Successfully Held in Jakarta（2026-04-30）[/LINK]",
        "application_method": "Applicants check www.campuschina.org for information about Chinese universities and scholarship programs, contact their preferred Chinese universities and obtain Pre-Admission Documents, then submit the online application using Indonesian Agency Number 3602. \"There is no need to send paper materials to the embassy.\" From 9 February to 5 March 2026 the embassy sends all recommended applications to the China Scholarship Council for final review. From July to August 2026 applicants check admission results in the system themselves; the embassy notifies winners to download the admission notice and JW201 visa form from the system.",
        "selection_notes": "{\"Eligibility screening against the published age, nationality, health, CSCA and HSK conditions\",\"Academic ability, language proficiency and other relevant criteria of the applied university\",\"The embassy screens and recommends; the China Scholarship Council performs final review\",\"No scoring, weighting or ranking method is published in the notice\"}",
