          "description": "The India Science and Research Fellowship (ISRF), run by the Department of Science and Technology through the Indian National Science Academy, gives researchers from Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Bhutan, Maldives, Myanmar, Nepal, Sri Lanka and Thailand a 3-6 month visiting fellowship at Indian research laboratories and academic institutions. Up to 80 fellowships are awarded each year, capped at 10 per country, and the award comprises an INR 50,000 monthly allowance plus contingency grants, round-trip economy airfare and a reimbursed visa fee. The 2025-2026 call opened on 31 December 2025 and closed on 31 March 2026.",
