            "Transcripts for every year of all university studies, organised chronologically from the most recent to the oldest",
            "A letter from the publisher for each submitted article and a notice from the editor for each accepted article, for the components that require it",
            "Attestation from the educational institution that the student is not subject to any interruption of studies or a suspension for semesters 1, 2 and 3",
            "Official attestation from the educational institution of an interrupted enrolment, along with a medical certificate, if applicable",
            "A copy of the doctoral diploma and the official transcript of study records, if applicable",
            "A letter of acceptance from the supervisor, submitted by the supervisor through FRQnet, where applicable",
            "A justification and supporting documents for any exception measure where the mandatory conditions are not met"
          ],
          "english_requirement": null,
          "english_requirement_note": "The PBEEE does not require an English language test. The program rules address only the language of forms and documents: 'Forms and documents must be completed in French. Documents written in a language other than French must be accompanied by a basic translation into French (Section 3.6 of the Common General Regulations).' The programme's official working language for applications is French, and no English score or level is published, so none is asserted here.",
          "selection_criteria": [
            "The excellence of the applications presented will be assessed by multidisciplinary evaluation committees composed of professors and university researchers",
            "Applications are evaluated according to the evaluation criteria and weighting published in the program rules, illustrated in the page image at https://frq.gouv.qc.ca/app/uploads/2025/08/capture-decran-2025-08-14-180258.png"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": null,
          "duration": "Component-dependent. VM: maximum 6 instalments, 2 years. Doctoral: up to 12 sessions, 3 years, with a reduced rate in sessions 10-12 if extended. Postdoctoral: not renewable, 3 instalments. Short-term: not renewable, maximum 4 instalments.",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "Must comply with the scholarship holder's guide to the applicable rules",
            "The start of the scholarship period must fall between 1 May 2026 and 15 January 2027; the scholarship is not retroactive and semesters prior to summer 2026 cannot be funded",
            "Scholarship payments only begin once the FRQ receives a copy of the study permit for doctoral candidates, or the work permit for postdoctoral candidates",
            "Must be dedicated full time to the research and to the research activities of the program",
            "Must be physically present in Québec for the entire duration of the scholarship and attend the host university, except for the short-term component and research stays outside Québec authorised by the FRQ",
            "Must comply with the scholarship terms and conditions regarding joint (cotutelle) degrees, concurrent scholarships, and part-time work with the supervisor's agreement",
            "Open access is required: the thesis and peer-reviewed publications produced with scholarship support must be accessible without embargo",
            "Must grant the MES and the FRQ a non-exclusive, irrevocable and non-transferable licence on the final report and research findings",
            "Must acknowledge the financial support of the MES in partnership with the FRQ in publications, notices and interviews"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "Component-specific supplementary scholarships for certain countries and institutions",
            "Responsibility of the MES - the scholarship is financed by the Ministère de l'Enseignement supérieur and the Fonds de recherche du Québec"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "programme_contact": "The program's contact module on the FRQ page, kossa@frq.gouv.qc.ca for certain program components",
            "funders": "Ministère de l'Enseignement supérieur (MES); Fonds de recherche du Québec (FRQ)"
          },
          "description": "The PBEEE (Programme de bourses d'excellence pour les étudiants étrangers) is a merit scholarship from the Québec Ministry of Higher Education and the Fonds de recherche du Québec for foreign students doing full-time research study in Québec, awarded in 14 sub-components. Amounts and duration vary by component, from a $3,000 per month short-term award to a doctoral award totalling up to $87,000 over three years, and the MES adds an exemption from higher foreign-student tuition fees plus RAMQ medical insurance. The 2026-2027 round is marked out of competition and candidates must be preselected by a Québec university, the CCTT network or the China Scholarship Council.",
          "program_type": "Government research scholarship for foreign students (Québec)",
          "region": "Québec, Canada",
          "coverage": "Covers a component-dependent stipend for up to three years, a French-language university tuition-fee exemption for foreign students, and RAMQ medical insurance; it does not cover travel, family or relocation costs, and the physical-presence requirement means applicants must live in Québec throughout.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Establish your preselection route first - a Québec university, the CCTT network or the China Scholarship Council - because only preselected candidates can enter the competition",
            "Apply to the university programme as a research master's, doctoral or postdoctoral study option; a professional master's, an essay or a literature review is ineligible",
            "Check your country of citizenship against the component-specific bilateral agreements with Brazil, China, India, Israel and Wallonia before choosing a component",
            "Confirm you are not a Canadian citizen or permanent resident and have not applied for Canadian permanent residence",
            "Time your start between 1 May 2026 and 15 January 2027, since the award is not retroactive",
            "Collect transcripts for every year of university study in chronological order, newest to oldest, with grading systems for non-North American institutions",
            "Line up your supervisor early, since for some components the supervisor submits the acceptance letter through FRQnet, not you",
            "Prepare all documents in French or with a French translation, as the forms and documents must be in French"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Not being preselected, which makes entry to the competition impossible regardless of academic strength",
            "Applying to a professional master's or a non-research study option",
            "Missing the earlier 23 October 2025 institutional nomination deadline, which is two months before the applicant deadline and is outside the applicant's control",
            "Being a Canadian citizen, permanent resident, or having applied for permanent residence",
            "Already having received a PBEEE",
            "Choosing a component whose bilateral agreement excludes your nationality",
            "Starting the study period before 1 May 2026 or after 15 January 2027, which makes earlier or later months unfundable",
            "Being a Québec, Wallonia or Maghreb candidate, who is ineligible, with Wallonia requiring prior study at a French-language Belgian institution",
            "Not being able to be physically present in Québec for the whole scholarship period"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Airfare to Québec and any travel, which the program does not list",
            "Relocation and family costs",
            "Room, board and everyday living costs beyond the stipend, which the program does not itemise",
            "Research consumables and equipment not covered by the supervisor or institution",
            "Any study costs before the 1 May 2026 start, which are explicitly unfundable"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Order transcripts newest to oldest as the rules specify, and include the grading system for any non-North-American transcript",
            "Attach publisher acknowledgements for submitted articles and editor notices for accepted articles where the component requires them",
            "If you have ever interrupted your studies, obtain both the official institutional attestation and a medical certificate, since either alone is insufficient",
            "Confirm your supervisor has actually submitted the acceptance letter through FRQnet for components that require it",
            "Include a justification and supporting documents for any exception measure, rather than assuming an exception will be granted"
          ],
          "alerts": [
            {
              "trigger": "23 October 2025",
              "message": "Guidance only: the earlier institutional nomination deadline for the responsible Québec entity. Your university or CCTT network must submit before this, so raise it with them at the start of your cycle."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "2 December 2025, 16:00 EST",
              "message": "Guidance only: the applicant submission deadline. Late submissions are not accepted under the Common General Regulations."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "1 May 2026",
              "message": "Guidance only: the earliest permitted scholarship start. Any semester before summer 2026 cannot be funded, so a September 2026 start is too late for that year."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Before submitting",
              "message": "Guidance only: payments do not begin until the FRQ receives your study permit (doctoral) or work permit (postdoctoral) copy, so permit delays delay your money."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "When planning outside research stays",
              "message": "Guidance only: the physical-presence-in-Québec requirement is strict. Only the short-term component and FRQ-authorised research stays outside Québec are excepted."
            }
          ],
          "submission_workflow": [
            "Identify your preselection route: a Québec university, the CCTT network or the China Scholarship Council",
            "Ask the responsible entity to submit the nomination form to the FRQ by 23 October 2025 at 4 p.m.",
            "Apply to a research master's, doctoral or postdoctoral study option under a regular-staff supervisor",
            "Choose a component compatible with your degree level and nationality",
            "Create your FRQnet account",
            "Wait for the FRQ to contact you, then complete the electronic form and attach all documents in French",
            "Submit electronically by 2 December 2025 at 4 p.m.",
            "Await assessment by multidisciplinary evaluation committees of professors and researchers",
            "On award, begin the scholarship period between 1 May 2026 and 15 January 2027 and apply for your study or work permit",
            "Accept the open access, licensing and acknowledgement conditions"
          ]
        },
        "programme_verification": {
          "cycle_verified": "PBEEE 2026-2027 fiscal year, marked 'These program rules are out of competition'",
          "verification_confidence": 0.87,
          "official_fields_confirmed": [
            "deadline_central (2 December 2025 at 16:00 EST) and deadline_institutional (23 October 2025 nomination date)",
            "status CLOSED and the out-of-competition banner",
            "the four component value tiers and their instalment caps",
            "tuition_coverage: the MES exemption from higher foreign-student tuition fees and RAMQ medical insurance",
            "the 14 sub-components and the bilateral country-of-citizenship restrictions",
            "eligibility including the Canadian citizenship and Quebec/Wallonia/Maghreb exclusions",
            "the full-time definition of at least 12 credits per half-year",
            "the thesis/dissertation/research report/article requirement and the exclusion of essays, literature reviews and professional master's programmes",
            "the non-retroactivity rule and the 1 May 2026 to 15 January 2027 start window",
            "the permit-gated payment condition",
            "open access, licensing and acknowledgement obligations"
          ],
          "institution_check_required": [
