          "research_requirement": "not required",
          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "Fellows are placed in cohorts by professional field across four impact areas: Human and Institutional Capacity, including economic development, finance and banking, public policy analysis and public administration, and technology policy and management; Rights and Freedoms, including communications or journalism and law and human rights; Sustainable Lands, including agricultural and rural development, natural resources, sustainability and environmental policy, and urban and regional planning; and Thriving Communities, including public health policy and management, substance abuse education, treatment and prevention, and educational administration, planning and policy.",
          "application_method": "Apply through the Binational Fulbright Commission or the Public Affairs Section of the US Embassy in the applicant's home country. US Embassies and Fulbright Commissions review and nominate candidates for further consideration by Washington-based selection panels.",
