            "funder": "U.S. Department of State, Bureau of Educational and Cultural Affairs"
          },
          "description": "The Hubert H. Humphrey Fellowship Program, a Fulbright exchange funded by the US Department of State and administered by IIE, provides 10 months of professional enrichment and non-degree graduate-level study in the United States for accomplished mid-level professionals from designated countries. Applicants are nominated by US Embassies or Fulbright Commissions, placed in professional-field groups at selected US universities, and complete a six-week professional affiliation, a required seminar and a Global Leadership Forum. Application deadlines vary by country and are set by the embassy or commission.",
