          "application_cycle": "Annual incoming offer; the recorded page is the 2024/2025 edition (Announcement No. 3 of 23 January 2024, as amended) and the current edition is Announcement No. 11/2026 of 10 March 2026 for the 2026/2027 academic year",
          "deadline_central": "2024-09-30T23:59",
          "deadline_central_display": "Applicants register (submit applications) in the Agency's IT System within the deadline specified in the message from the Agency sent electronically, but no later than September 30, 2024.",
          "deadline_central_timezone": "Europe/Warsaw",
          "deadline_institutional": "2024-06-30T23:59",
          "deadline_note": "The recorded page is the closed 2024/2025 edition. Its pipeline is: candidates apply to partner institutions in their own country under their own rules; foreign partner institutions must submit lists of recommended candidates to NAWA by 30 June 2024; after receiving those lists NAWA contacts applicants with the method and date of registration; and the applicant must register in NAWA's IT System by the deadline given in that message and in any case no later than 30 September 2024. Candidates from Germany applied directly to NAWA by email by 30 June 2024 under the NAWA-DAAD agreement. The current 2026/2027 edition is Announcement No. 11/2026 of 10 March 2026 and its deadline sits in the announcement PDF, which I could not parse.",
          "status": "CLOSED",
          "status_note": "The recorded 2024/2025 edition is closed: applications were due by 30 September 2024 and results were announced by 31 December 2024. The current 2026/2027 edition (Announcement No. 11/2026 of 10 March 2026) is the live cycle, and the programme site lists call results for it, so it is also past its application stage.",
          "funding_amount": 2000,
          "funding_currency": "PLN",
          "funding_period": "per month",
          "funding_duration": "maximum 10 months per academic year for preparatory course participants and first-cycle, second-cycle and long-cycle master's students; maximum 12 months per academic year for doctoral school students",
          "tuition_coverage": true,
          "tuition_coverage_note": "For students, the scholarship of the Director of NAWA also includes exemption from fees for education at preparatory courses or at public universities supervised by the Minister of Science and Higher Education. Costs of participation in preparatory courses in Polish and in education are covered by the Polish party. Tuition treatment depends on whether the bilateral agreement makes Poland the paying party; where the sending party pays, terms follow that agreement.",
          "living_cost_coverage": true,
          "travel_coverage": true,
          "fully_funded": false,
          "funding_label": "PLN 2,000 per month for students and preparatory course participants (from 1 January 2026), PLN 2,500 for doctoral students on research stays, PLN 3,500 for doctoral degree holders, plus tuition exemption",
          "benefits": [
            "Monthly scholarship paid through the host university where Poland is the paying party: PLN 2,000 per month for preparatory course participants and for students of first-cycle, second-cycle and long-cycle master's degree programmes, effective 1 January 2026 under Announcement No. 47/2025 of 17 December 2025",
            "PLN 2,500 per month for doctoral students on research stays and PLN 3,500 per month for doctoral degree holders",
            "Doctoral school students receive the scholarship amount resulting from Article 209 of the Act on Higher Education and Science",
            "Exemption from fees for preparatory courses or study at public universities supervised by the Minister of Science and Higher Education, for students",
            "Travel costs to Poland, since the announcement states costs of participation in preparatory courses in Polish and in education are covered by the Polish party"
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Secondary school graduates who, at the time of starting their education in Poland, hold a school leaving certificate giving them the right to undertake studies in the country of issue in any field and type of university",
            "Students",
            "University graduates applying for admission to the next level of education who obtained a diploma no earlier than 2022 (for the 2024/2025 edition)",
            "People with the status of a doctoral student in accordance with the principles of the higher education and science system of their country",
            "Scientists and academic teachers conducting research or teaching in a country participating in the Programme who are not employed in a Polish institution of the higher education and science system",
            "Be a national of a country listed in Appendix 1 to the Announcement, and hold a form of stay that country's offer actually provides"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Nationals of partner countries covered by bilateral agreements with Poland, listed in Appendix 1 to the Announcement. The list differs by country and by scholarship years, and the 2024/2025 edition named Yemen, Palestine, Rwanda, Thailand, Taiwan, Ukraine, Bulgaria, Japan, Kazakhstan, Germany and Slovakia among those amended.",
          "international_eligibility": "Explicit: the programme is for incoming students, doctoral students, academic teachers and scientists from the partner countries named in Appendix 1, and the form of stay available depends on the bilateral agreement with that country.",
          "degree_levels": [
            "Bachelor's",
            "Master's",
            "Long-cycle Master's",
            "Doctoral",
            "Postdoctoral"
          ],
          "study_mode": "full-time",
          "research_requirement": "required",
          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "Open to students, doctoral students and employees of universities and research institutes representing all fields of science, unless a given international agreement provides otherwise. Applicants present one or more planned activities, their goals, their importance, and the justification for the chosen Polish host centre.",
          "application_method": "Three-stage route. First, apply to a partner institution in your own country under its rules and deadlines. Second, the foreign partner institution submits a list of recommended candidates to NAWA, containing name, surname, gender, date of birth, e-mail, intended Polish host centre and form of stay. Third, after receiving the lists, NAWA contacts applicants with the method and date of registration, and the applicant registers in NAWA's IT System. Applicants from Germany applied individually to NAWA by email under the NAWA-DAAD agreement. Applicants for full-cycle education also take part in recruitment at their chosen Polish university, which NAWA does not administer.",
          "application_route": "partner-institution",
          "requirements": [
            "Apply to a partner institution in your own country under that institution's rules and deadlines",
            "Be recommended by the foreign partner institution, which must submit its list to NAWA by 30 June 2024 in the recorded edition",
            "Register and submit the application in NAWA's IT System by the notified deadline and no later than 30 September 2024 in the recorded edition",
            "Submit only one application per call under the Programme; if more than one is submitted, the last one in the recruitment process is assessed",
            "For full-cycle education, apply independently to a Polish university through the universities' electronic registration system within the deadlines set for foreigners, since NAWA does not take part in university recruitment",
            "For research stays and part-time studies, contact the Polish host centre yourself to confirm the stay is possible, as the final decision is made by the host centre",
            "Study only at host centres supervised by the Minister of Science and Higher Education"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "For full-cycle education: a secondary school leaving certificate giving the right to undertake first-cycle studies in the country of its issue, or a list of grades for the last semester for final-year secondary students; a copy of the first-cycle studies diploma giving the right to undertake second-cycle studies, or a transcript of grades for final-year first-cycle students",
            "For part-time studies: a copy of the diploma or a transcript of grades from the previous course of study; a CV of no more than 2 pages; a cover letter justifying the choice of host centre in Poland; a copy of confirmation of admission to part-time studies by the Polish host centre or an invitation; a recommendation from an academic teacher at the home university; confirmation of knowledge of Polish or a foreign language at at least B1 level",
            "For doctoral school study or research stays: a research plan describing the planned activities and the justification for the selection; a copy of the highest diploma obtained; a CV including publications, ongoing research projects, foreign internships and special achievements, maximum 3 pages; a copy of confirmation of admission to the type of stay applied for, or an invitation, issued by the Polish host centre; a recommendation from an independent researcher, not required for PhD holders or professors; confirmation of knowledge of Polish or a foreign language at at least B1 level"
          ],
          "english_requirement": "Confirmation of knowledge of Polish or a foreign language at at least B1 level, enabling communication with the host centre in Poland",
          "english_requirement_note": "The recorded announcement requires a confirmation of Polish or a foreign language at at least B1 level for part-time study, doctoral school study and research stays, and states that the application must be completed in Polish or English with appendices in Polish or English, other languages translated, and that a doctoral diploma copy in Latin is accepted. No specific English test or score is required.",
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Applications in NAWA's IT System undergo formal assessment against three criteria: submission via a foreign partner institution from the applicant's country; compatibility of the application with the offer for the applicant's country; and registration with all required attachments described in point 2.6",
            "Applications are verified against the limits of places, types and lengths of stays stated in Appendix 1",
            "Applicants present one or more intended activities with their goals, their importance for the studies or scientific career, and the justification for the chosen host centre"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": null,
          "duration": "For full-cycle education, the statutory duration of the education cycle in Poland, and studies may be preceded by a one-year preparatory course in Polish. Permissible lengths of stay are stated per country in Appendix 1. The stay should be continuous; for part-time studies and research stays, time outside the host facility may not exceed one fifth of the entire stay.",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "Implement the study programme, scientific, teaching or other activity indicated in the application, continuously during the stay",
            "Submit a final report in NAWA's IT System within 30 days of the end of the stay, with a certificate from the host centre confirming completion of the stay",
            "Students continuing into the next academic year must submit annual reports, in the amended 2024/2025 rules by 31 October each year, in the form of a host certificate with the grade point average and confirmation of enrolment; failure to report may be a basis for withholding payment",
            "Failure to submit the final report may ground a demand for repayment and exclusion from the next NAWA call",
            "Immediately inform NAWA of changes in the implementation of the project",
            "Include the full name of the Polish National Agency for Academic Exchange in Polish or English on all publications resulting from the stay",
            "Sign the scholarship agreement in NAWA's IT System within 30 days of it being made available; the agreement is concluded only after a positive formal assessment, acceptance by the Polish host centre and the Director's final decision",
            "The programme implementation cannot be combined with another scholarship from other sources, including an EU Erasmus+ scholarship",
            "For research stays, to receive the full monthly rate the holder must stay at the host facility for at least 15 days in any 30 consecutive days; shorter stays receive half the rate"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "One-year NAWA preparatory Polish language course, with the centre assigned by NAWA based on field of study and place availability",
            "Doctoral school education as a distinct form of stay",
            "Part-time studies, research stays and scientific internships for academic teachers and scientists"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "Polish National Agency for Academic Exchange (NAWA), Department of Programmes for Students, Bilateral Programmes Unit, ul. Polna 40, 00-635 Warsaw; +48 451 058 639; +48 451 058 635; +48 22 390 35 00"
          },
          "description": "The Zawacka NAWA Programme is the incoming strand of Poland's bilateral scholarship offer, bringing students, doctoral students, academic teachers and scientists from partner countries to Polish higher education and science institutions. Candidates are nominated by a partner institution in their own country, which submits a list to NAWA, and then register in NAWA's IT System. Students receive PLN 2,000 per month and exemption from fees at public universities supervised by the Minister of Science and Higher Education, while doctoral research stays receive PLN 2,500 and doctoral degree holders PLN 3,500. Whether NAWA or the sending party pays depends on each bilateral agreement; in the 2024/2025 round NAWA paid for candidates from North Macedonia, Moldova and Serbia.",
